From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Seeed Studio <support@seeed.cc>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: rk3588: boot through balena environment

The vendor default boots through the RKIMG/Android path.  Balena needs
to select the flasher or active root partition and construct the kernel
command line before running distro boot, which then locates the
generated extlinux.conf.

Regenerated for the radxa next-dev-v2024.10 tree: the radxa header
carries an "#undef CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND" line above the RKIMG define that
the original SDK-tree patch did not have in its context.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [configuration]
---
diff --git a/include/configs/evb_rk3588.h b/include/configs/evb_rk3588.h
index 737ee68..7b38c5e 100644
--- a/include/configs/evb_rk3588.h
+++ b/include/configs/evb_rk3588.h
@@ -19,7 +19,11 @@
 #define CONFIG_SYS_MMC_ENV_DEV		0
 
 #undef CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND
-#define CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND RKIMG_BOOTCOMMAND
+#define CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND \
+    "setenv resin_kernel_load_addr ${kernel_addr_r};" \
+    "run resin_set_kernel_root;" \
+    "run set_os_cmdline;" \
+    "run distro_bootcmd;"
 
 #endif
 #endif
\ No newline at end of file
